[
    {
        "content": "<p>If a instance is proved by <code>inferInstance</code>, do we need it in Mathlib. For example, </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NumberTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LocalField</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RingTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Valuation</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Discrete</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ValuativeRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsNonarchimedeanLocalField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ValuativeRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Valued</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">integer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsNonarchimedeanLocalField</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WithZero</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsCyclic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroupWithZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Units</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">valueGroupWithZeroIsoInt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMulEquiv</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isCyclic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nontrivial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroupWithZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ValuativeRel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isNontrivial_iff_nontrivial_units</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ValuativeRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">UniformSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsUniformAddGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsNonarchimedeanLocalField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> without the two instances above, inferInstance fails. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Valued</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsRankOneDiscrete</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>1) do we already have these three instance in Mathlib. 2) The third instance is directly followed by <code>inferInstance</code>. I was wondering whether we need to write down this in mathlib. Refer: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38251\">#38251</a>. My motivation to do this is that we can pick an uniformizer in <code>𝒪[K]</code> using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Valuation/Discrete/Basic.html#Valuation.Uniformizer\"><code>Valuation.Uniformizer</code></a>. Thanks in advance!</p>",
        "id": 587713281,
        "sender_full_name": "Wenrong Zou",
        "timestamp": 1776676044
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can write <code>#synth (Valued.v (R := K)).IsRankOneDiscrete</code> on an empty line, to learn which instance Lean already knows about.</p>",
        "id": 587718190,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776677433
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, I know that it use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Valuation/Discrete/Basic.html#Valuation.IsRankOneDiscrete.mk'\"><code>Valuation.IsRankOneDiscrete.mk'</code></a>, so I provide two instances above.</p>",
        "id": 587720277,
        "sender_full_name": "Wenrong Zou",
        "timestamp": 1776677922
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The question to your answer (1) is: Write <code>import Mathlib</code> at the top of your file, and try <code>#synth</code>.<br>\nRe (2): Usually we don't have instances explicitly if <code>inferInstance</code> finds them. There are some technical reasons (instance shortcuts) to sometimes have them. But this doesn't seem to be one.</p>",
        "id": 587720956,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776678115
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 587721300,
        "sender_full_name": "Wenrong Zou",
        "timestamp": 1776678224
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Re: After writing <code>import Mathlib</code> at the top of the file, <code>#synth</code> tells us <code>Valuation.IsRankOneDiscrete.mk' Valued.v</code> as we expected.</p>",
        "id": 587721727,
        "sender_full_name": "Wenrong Zou",
        "timestamp": 1776678358
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"641254\">@Wenrong Zou</span>, there is an ongoing refactor to remove <code>Valued</code> from Mathlib in favor of <code>ValuativeRel</code>, so you should avoid building new results over <code>Valued</code>.</p>",
        "id": 587782397,
        "sender_full_name": "María Inés de Frutos Fernández",
        "timestamp": 1776695553
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks!</p>",
